MMALDecode - H.264 decoded by the VideoCore, from RISC OS
=========================================================

Step 3 towards hardware H.264 decoding in Reel on every Raspberry Pi
from the Pi 1 to the Pi 4. MMALProbe showed the firmware's video decoder
answers through RISC OS's VCHIQ module; this makes it decode.

For each of three clips (in clips):
  small  640x360, 60 pictures, H.264 Main with B frames
  odd    426x240, 30 pictures, H.264 Baseline (a width that isn't a
         multiple of 32, to check the cropping)
  hd     1920x1080, 150 pictures, H.264 High, level 4.1

it sets the decoder up, sends the stream to the VideoCore, takes every
decoded picture back, and checks each one against a checksum FFmpeg made
of the same picture with its own decoder. H.264 decoders must agree to
the last bit, so any difference is a fault. It also times the decode.

Running it:
  Double-click Test. It runs the three clips one after another (the hd
  one takes a few seconds) and writes Result in this directory. Please
  send Result back, and one from an older Pi (1, 2, 3 or Zero) too if
  you can.

  If Test doesn't get pictures back, double-click Verbose too: it runs
  the small clip only, writing every message to and from the decoder to
  ResultV. Please send that as well.

The decoded pictures come back to RISC OS by the VCHIQ module's bulk
transfer, and a nine-instruction callback in the RMA counts them in; it's
removed at the end. If the machine locks up (it shouldn't), switch it off
and on again.

Needs: RISC OS 5 on a Raspberry Pi, with the VCHIQ module (in the ROM).
Part of riscos-ffmpeg; MIT licence. The clips are made from FFmpeg's
testsrc2 pattern.
